         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/59e6973f-013a-44bf-9546-408b4ef38e15,1794426766585/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C303%2C5825%2C3276%29%3B' alt='Chief Myron Demkiw stands in front of a wall decorated with Toronto police logos during a news conference.' width='620' height='349' title='Chief Myron Demkiw and Det.-Sgt. Stacey McCabe update members of the media on a shooting and homicide investigation at the Salsa on St. Clair festival, at police headquarters, in Toronto, on Aug. 7, 2026.'/><p>Toronto police currently operate four community safety hubs in the city. Police Chief Myron Demkiw recently announced he was pausing applications for more while the force works out where they can deploy them effectively as a deterrent.</p>]]></description>
